==Battleground==
*6 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*6 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*2 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Casaurian Ahirujo]] spawns after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Vermilingua Rangmaster]] spawns as the boss.
**9 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn, delay 2.67~6 seconds<sup>80f~180f</sup>.
**15 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**5 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
**10 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] is easily able to kill everything before the base is hit. Arguably the biggest threat after such is not the Vermilingua Rangmaster, but the 24 Sinner Snaches that spawn with it, as the [[Surge Attack#Death Surge|Death Surge]]s they spawn can easily clear your defenses. Strong meatshielding is vital to keep them as well as all the other enemies at bay. After the Sinner Snache spam has ceased, no more peons will be spawned, leaving Rangmaster alone and easy to attack. Units like [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic King Dragon Cat]] that outrange Rangmaster will make the cleanup phase easy. [[Li'l King Dragon Cat]] with the Surge Immunity Talent is better able to stack up than other options, as it is unharmed by the Sinner Snaches' Death Surges.

